        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ef8f4f35250f4d7982c7743f69b6f6a6",
      "statement": "The extraction schema deliberately contains no identifier grammar, classification enum, regex taxonomy or per-corpus keyword list, and the page-kind list describes what a sheet of paper is rather than what this corpus contains — a model-returned kind outside the list is normalised rather than re-billing the window.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L6-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6f669002cfc8dc7a6c937d286324fbbbb1cdbddd630079ce8f5de48963e1d3f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L60-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bbd61462ed99c99ddcf6a20f7ee3c0960b904d8af89ae9ca7cc810c4384446c4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6111ca11c5e247f9b7bad0c6f4efb862",
      "statement": "Extraction asks for section presence per page and never for extent, because a fold can cut through a section and the model on one side cannot see the other, so any span it reported would be a confident guess.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L15-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76e019afde3f9aa734e9019da2f55820f50549004d8f4beea5577520cee1287e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27aee44002ef4cfb85dbd23bfdbcd722",
      "statement": "The model returns structure and codes but never page text, because the text comes from the PDF library at the probe step — which is what makes the next step able to check the model's codes against what is actually printed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L22-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a238bf2691ab0458b048d1caee38a09fd1f8ac484df55244d68c19f8fc68d61:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eb0348029ecc43fba98383b3155ab798",
      "statement": "What is cached is the verbatim response body rather than the derived page record, so every downstream derivation change can be re-run for free instead of requiring the paid call to be bought again.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L27-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47282c1ec36dfff66c0f96cee3b9288fbf4aaff6cb3a80639370b504a6abcb7b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52934817418648aea7f1b68d91e8199e",
      "statement": "Four triggers bisect a window and re-bill it — the output ceiling, an unterminated body, a schema-invalid body, and a page-index set that is not exactly 1..N — and the pipeline never pads, never guesses the offset and never accepts a partial window.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L268-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fc3e49fc9ce6f8cbcc763601aa38f835ccbfc6ed5f2621fdc681fd506d69a1e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L33-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f71a6094506ee429c4eda8265ae8e99d3188e1ce4ae80f49a27d4b661f4e697c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_74b86ab0e335444b8aa5f00b121b812c",
      "statement": "Bisection's floor is a single page, which raises a typed unsplittable-window refusal; there is no recursion-depth counter, because the terminus is that page rather than a limit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L36-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:251806a2f234c54e83ded0f078cecbcc009f03b30ed4ca2caf18c413e220fce3:"
