        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fcaf90f78f4846758ae0022b8fdae1b1",
      "statement": "The structural offset check requires the window's page indices to be exactly 1..N each once, and is implemented by one function shared between extraction and derivation so a single function owns the question.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/extract.py#L241-L265",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48d273caf243b6f8f3f507c83c948e01d0eebc26c779021eecb6a34a26ee24b2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1af0b40297cf49b5a985fb5115c86b87",
      "statement": "The structural check runs before the observational one because an index set that is not 1..N makes the absolute page of every form meaningless, leaving nothing sound for the second check to run on.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/derive.py#L240-L245",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f7d8afebf4580995456ccf0eb0e46c407b46eac27d13d1ad920ce3db6ca0a275:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d133460a65df4fbd9ab7845a1dc63893",
      "statement": "The observational offset check classifies every page of the window into three states — confirms itself, witness, or printed nowhere — and the printed-nowhere case is evidence of nothing, because on one legacy window 29 of 30 labels are printed nowhere and counting them as agreement would silence the one page that can see.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/derive.py#L246-L257",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4695d406d4cb108715487e00697621d4c0268959545de809ddb9a010cfa3d83b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2ed2c091d2974181a25d4c6e0ca6a950",
      "statement": "A window is refused for offset when witnesses reach two, or when there is one witness and no page confirms its own label — the second clause being necessary so that bisecting a genuinely shifted window reaches the unsplittable refusal instead of terminating by accepting its single pages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/derive.py#L258-L269",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ce984a760f87e5fe078c40254e4b820983f9e57011c9c6738f1a34f56e20f30:"
